        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Take the smaller of the powers of 2 and 5. Each pair $2\\cdot5=10$ gives one trailing zero.",
          "worked": "Count the pairs of factors 2 and 5: their number is the smaller of the two indices. Each pair makes a factor of 10. Multiplying a whole number by 10 appends one zero, so the number of pairs is the number of trailing zeros.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many zeroes are on the end of $2^{100}\\cdot3^{40}\\cdot5^{80}$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "80 trailing zeros.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{100}\\cdot3^{40}\\cdot5^{80} &= 2^{20}\\cdot3^{40}\\cdot(2\\cdot5)^{80}\\\\2^{100}\\cdot3^{40}\\cdot5^{80} &= 2^{20}\\cdot3^{40}\\cdot10^{80}\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 80 pairs of factors 2 and 5, so there are 80 trailing zeros.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
